<newsitem itemid="453014" id="root" date="1997-03-19" xml:lang="en">
<title>HONG KONG: Mandarin Oriental 1996 net US$60.1 mln.</title>
<headline>Mandarin Oriental 1996 net US$60.1 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31.</p>
<p>				(million US$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)		   8.66    vs     7.78</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)    4.65    vs     4.35</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)    6.30    vs     5.90</p>
<p>    Pretax			  73.3     vs    63.0</p>
<p>    Net attributable profit   60.1     vs    53.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		     227.2     vs   192.0</p>
<p>NOTE - Luxury hotel operator Mandarin Oriental International Ltd said positive trends at the group's Hong Kong and Manila hotels had continued into 1997. With overall improvement anticipated in the performance of the group's other Asian hotels and the Hyde Park in London expected to make a positive contribution to group profits in its first full year, the outlook for 1997 is &quot;encouraging&quot;.</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    74.1     vs    55.5</p>
<p>    Net interest expense	 8.2     vs     4.8</p>
<p>    Retained profit	     16.3     vs     12.9</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6346</p>
</text>
